title: 'pallet-broker: do not consume unsettled timeslices in claim_revenue'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    `claim_revenue` advanced a pool contribution past a timeslice before checking whether its
    revenue could be paid out, so claiming before a timeslice was settled lost that timeslice's
    payout. It now stops at the first timeslice whose revenue has not yet been reported, or which
    has not yet been committed, and keeps the remaining contribution so the claim can be retried.
    A history entry missing at or before the last committed timeslice is still treated as dropped.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: patch
